Playwright
1. Playwright is webbased application automation tool like selenium and cypress
2. Playwright supports - webbased application, webbrowser mobile(web apps -facebook,linkedin)
3. Doesn't automate native mobile application (android and IOS) like cypress
4. Appium tools use to automate for mobile native application
5. Playwright supports - java, javascripts, typescripts ,c#, python, .net
6. playwright invented by microsoft in 2020
7. Browser support in playwright - safari, chrome, firefox.
8. OS - window, linux, IOS, CLI


Feature of playwright
1. free and open source.
2. very easy to install playwright
3. functional, API, accessibility testing (cypress)
4. parallel-testing
5. Auto-wait mechanism
6. Build in assertion (javascripts)
7. virtual devices execution supported in playwright
8. fast - very fast
9. does support iframe and shadow feature....


How to run the test in playwright
1. npx playwright test | headless mode | runs all testcases in headless mode
2. npx playwright test --headed | runs all testcases without headless mode 
3. npx playwright show-report | to open reports on browser.
4. npx playwright test "filename" (examples.spec.js)" | to run test from specific file..
5. npx playwright test "fileName" --headed --project=chromium|webkit|firefox | to run testcases on specific browsers.
6. npx playwright test --ui | to enable and run the test in playwright from UI.
7. npx playwright test "filename" (examples.spec.js) --ui | to enable and run the specific test in playwright from UI.
8. npx playwright test "filename" --headed --porject=chromium --debug | enable the debugger in playwright



